// A labelled block carrying a value (owner ruling 2026-09-29): its type is the join of its
// tail and every `break @B v`, here both `i32`, so the value is plain `i32`. The block is
// written inline at each delivery position, so the rewrite that lowers it runs everywhere
// the value can land. The proof prints the `break` value, which only the break path yields.
//
// Format: scripts/capability-probes/matrix.py, whose docstring is the spec.
// @@PRELUDE@@
function seven(): i32 { 7 }
// @@VALUE@@
@B { if seven() > 3 { break @B seven() * 2 }; 0 }
// @@TYPE@@
i32
// @@PROOF@@
print(v)
// @@WANT@@
14
// @@TEST@@
v > 10
// @@HIT@@
print(v)
// @@MISS@@
print("miss")
